# Language models
- 08 bow: each position averages all earlier positions (causal mask)
- 09 self-attention: learned weighted average (q/k/v), positional embeddings
- 10 transformer: multi-head, feed-forward, residual, layernorm, stacked blocks
- 11 bpe: tokenizer (train merges, encode, decode)
- 12 gpt: transformer on bpe tokens, scaled up, temperature / top-k sampling

# Mixture of experts (on top of 12)
- 13 moe: several feed-forward experts + softmax router (every expert used)
- 14 topk moe: route each token to top-k experts + load-balancing loss
- 15 shared moe: always-on shared experts + routed experts
- 16 upcycling: start an moe from a trained dense gpt's feed-forward weights
- 17 multi-token prediction: extra heads predicting t+2, t+3 (works on dense or moe)

# Generative models (images, independent of the above)
- 18 vae: encoder -> latent -> decoder, reparameterisation, kl loss
- 19 gan: generator vs discriminator

# Reinforcement learning
- 20 rl: policy gradient (reinforce) on a small toy environment
- 21 sft: fine-tune gpt on prompt -> answer pairs
- 22 rl gpt: policy gradient on gpt with a checkable reward (grpo style)
- 23 thinking gpt: reward correct final answers, let it learn to reason first
- 24 rl moe: rl on the moe model, routing stability
